OL,2,V55555555CECUADOR'S REBEL
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CGENERAL UNDER SIEGE
OL,4,B
OL,5, Ecuador's armed forces chief-of-staff
OL,6, is said to be holed up in an air force
OL,7, base after a failed mutiny.
OL,9, President Leon Febres Cordero said that
OL,10, the armed forces had remained loyal and
OL,11, he demanded the resignation of rebel
OL,12, Lt Gen Frank Vargas Pazos.
OL,14, But Vargas Pazos refused to step down
OL,15, and took refuge in the Manta base,
OL,16, which has now been surrounded by
OL,17, government troops.
OL,19, He said he had the backing of the air
OL,20, force and the navy but the president
OL,21, denied this.
