OL,2,V55555555CIRISH LEADERS IN
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CROW OVER ACCORD
OL,5, Dublin prime minister Garret FitzGerald
OL,6, and Fianna Fail opposition leader
OL,7, Charles Haughey are in a bitter row
OL,8, over the Anglo-Irish Ulster accord.
OL,10, Dr FitzGerald has accused Mr Haughey of
OL,11, "national sabotage" by criticising the
OL,12, agreement in New York.
OL,14, But Mr Haughey hit back, accusing the
OL,15, prime minister of "an hysterical
OL,16, outburst" in response to "restrained
OL,17, and responsible" remarks.
OL,19, Dr FitzGerald said that Mr Haughey's
OL,20, remarks were ill-timed because of the
OL,21, imminent arrival of US aid for Ireland.
